        "## **Project Proposal**\n",
        "---\n",
        "**Problem Statement & User**\n",
        "- Problem: Many music listeners want to know more about the music they are listening to, whether that be information about a song's artist, duration, or even popularity and chart performance. This model would traverse through music from the Billboard Hot 100 database in order to give users easy access to the latest popular tracks and their data as well as apparent trends in music over the years.\n",
        "- Target Users: This tool is useful for anywhere from casual music listeners who want to know more information about the music they are listening to to music data analysts who need the information to better understand tracks and their data.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Why AI / LLM?**\n",
        "- An LLM-based system is appropriate for this problem because it will be able to understand the natural written language queries of casual music fans, outputting responses that are actually readable and easy for all to understand. In addition, an LLM is able to utilize the data from a dataset and output a response that takes into account many different pieces of information from various sources at once through RAG and tool implementation.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Example Interactions**\n",
        "- Example 1:\n",
        "  - User: \"How many weeks was the song Easy on Me by Adele on the Billboard's Hot 100?\"\n",
        "  - System: \"The song Easy on Me by Adele was on the Billboard's Hot 100 for 3 weeks.\"\n",
        "\n",
        "- Example 2:\n",
        "  - User: \"What songs peaked at a rank of 2 in November of 2021?\"\n",
        "  - System: \"The song Bad Habits peaked at number 2 on the Billboard's Hot 100 on November 6th, 2021.\"\n",
        "\n",
        "**Data Source**\n",
        "- \"Billboard The Hot 100 Songs\" from Kaggle: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/dhruvildave/billboard-the-hot-100-songs\n",
        "\n",
        "**Key Improvements in This Version**\n",
        "- ✅ Metadata-filtered retrieval (replaces row-based chunking)\n",
        "- ✅ Improved confidence calculation with 3-factor scoring\n",
        "- ✅ User modes for casual listeners vs. data scientists\n",
        "- ✅ Stricter system prompts to reduce hallucination\n",
        "- ✅ Last.fm validation support\n",
        "- ✅ Increased TOP_K from 3 to 10 for better multi-song queries\n",
        "- ✅ New tool: artist appearance counter\n",
        "- ✅ Enhanced Gradio UI with confidence indicators"
      ],
